Hello.

Please see and comments attached patch against initial code imported
to netfilter CVS by Harald Welte <laforge@netfilter.org>.
This patch includes patch from Piotr Gasid'o<quaker@ondraszek.eu.org> 
to fix multiple -m matching with OSF, wich
was posted to mailing list yesterday, but contains a typo.

This patch also adds possibility to dynamically load fingerprints(for
complete list of supported fingerprints please see
http://www.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/etc/pf.os and
http://lcamtuf.coredump.cx/p0f.shtml) through /proc interface.

Examples:
loading new rule:
echo "16384:64:0:44:M512:.:AIX:4.3.2 and earlier">/proc/sys/net/ipv4/osf
For documentation about this magic string please see p0f.fp in p0f
((c) Michal Zalewski (lcamtuf@coredump.cx))
distribution(http://lcamtuf.coredump.cx/p0f.shtml)

reading loaded rules(not in loading format, but for info
about genries/details only): 
cat /proc/sys/net/ipv4/osf

All rules are added to linked list(with proper locking) without any
check, if this rule already exists.

One can drop whole fingerprint table with the following command:
echo -en FLUSH > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/osf

For loading from file one can use attached script(osf_load.sh):
osf_load.sh osf.fp /proc/sys/net/ipv4/osf

Any feedback is allways appreciated.

	Evgeniy Polyakov

